            <ArticleTitle>Portal vein thrombosis after splenectomy for beta-thalassemia major.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>225-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Portal vein thrombosis is a recognized complication after splenectomy in beta-thalassemia major due to the chronic hypercoagulable state which has been recognized to exist in childhood thalassemia and contribute to thromboembolic events. We are reporting one patient with beta-thalassemia major developed portal vein thrombosis following splenectomy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
